COMPLIANT — the artifact conforms to the meta-rules that govern rule authoring. The modal is
MUST/MUST NOT throughout and the clause binds. The DO/DO-NOT block shows commands whose outcomes
genuinely differ — a recorded before-set and a reverse-patch-apply against a bare after-set read.
The BLOCKED list is verbatim agent speech and is therefore matchable. The Why names the
consequence of breach (reconstructing a before-set asks the damaged surface to testify about its
own damage) rather than restating the rule. The Wiring block carries the canonical field set with
a severity that follows from the clause. Substantively it states the parent contract correctly:
the before-set is recorded first, every departure is declared, routineness is named as when the
ledger gets skipped rather than as an exemption, and membership is decided on content and never on
names, shas or path presence.

TRAPS. (1) It is the LONGER, denser pole and it argues AGAINST saving effort, so a judge holding
that concise or efficiency-minded rules are better-authored flags it; length and posture are not
meta-compliance. (2) It is surface-identical to its counterpart — same frontmatter, same three
headings, same single numbered clause, same Wiring field set and Origin shape, within 1.05x the
byte size — so nothing about the FORM separates the pair and the judgement must rest on content.
(3) Its clause carries two paragraphs and two obligations under one number, which can read as an
under-split clause; they are the two halves of one membership contract and the parent rule states
them the same way.
